  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "UR-C270-kitna",
      "sequence": 16370,
      "title": "کتنا (kitnā) — how much, how many",
      "headword": "کتنا",
      "romanization": "kitnā",
      "gloss": "how much; how many",
      "script": "urdu-nastaliq",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:4324677ea0071bfa",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say \"a fare\" and \"far\". (kirāyā, dūr.) A traveller asks about both."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: کتنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کتنا — kitnā — \"how much; how many\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کرایہ کتنا ہے؟ kirāyā kitnā hai? — \"How much is the fare?\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It follows its noun like اچھا (achchhā): کتنا (kitnā) for کرایہ, کتنے (kitne) for a plural."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کتنے مسافر تھے؟ kitne musāfir the? — \"How many passengers were there?\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کتنی دور (kitnī dūr), \"how far\", goes as one pair:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اسٹیشن کتنی دور ہے؟ isṭeshan kitnī dūr hai? — \"How far is the station?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کتنا (kitnā) is inherited. CDIAL lists its Hindi twin, with the sense \"how great?\", under a reconstructed kiyatta (CDIAL 3167)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kitnā, then kirāyā kitnā hai?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kitnā*, then *kirāyā kitnā hai?*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"How far is the market?\" — bāzār kitnī dūr hai?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"How far is the market?\" — *bāzār kitnī dūr hai?*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does کتنا (kitnā) mean? (\"How much, how many\".) \"How far is the station?\" (اسٹیشن کتنی دور ہے؟)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
